==Finnish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|ka|to}}
* {{rhymes|ɑto|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkɑto]}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably the source of {{term|kadota||to disappear|lang=fi}}, cognate with Estonian {{term|kadu||loss|lang=et}}.

{{etystub}}

====Noun====
{{fi-noun|ka|type=mato}}

# [[failure|Failure]] of [[crop]]s.
# [[loss|Loss]], [[disappearance]], [[lack]]; used primarily in compound terms.
#: ''[[yleisö]]'''kato''''' = lack or loss of audience

=====Declension=====
{{fi-decl-valo|ka|t|d}}

=====Derived terms=====
* verbs: [[kadota]]

=====Compounds=====
* [[katokorvaus]]
* [[katovahinko]]
* [[katovuosi]]
* [[kulmakarvakato]]
* [[silmäripsikato]]
* [[yleisökato]]

===Etymology 2===
A dialectal or colloquial 2nd person imperative present of {{term|katsoa||to look|lang=fi}}. The corresponding infinitive is {{term|kattoa}}.

====Verb====
'''kato'''

# {{colloquial|lang=fi}} [[look]]!
#: '''''Kato''', tuolla on George!'' &mdash; ''Look, there's George!''
# {{colloquial|lang=fi}} [[see]] (used often with [[nyt|ny]])
#: '''''Kato''' ny, mähän sanoin.'' &mdash; ''See, I told you so.''

=====Synonyms=====
* [[katso]]

====Interjection====
{{fi-int}}

# {{colloquial|lang=fi}} [[see]] or [[look]].
#* ''Se on '''kato''' sillä lailla.''
#** '''''See''', that’s the way it is.''
#* '''''Kato''' nääs!'' or '''''Kato kato!'''''
#** Literally: ''Look, look!.'' Uttered in surprise, not necessarily telling anyone to look anywhere.
#* ''...'''kato''' nääs.'' or ''...'''kato.'''''
#** ''...you see.'' (At the end of a sentence)

=====Synonyms=====
* [[katsos]], [[näet]], [[nimittäin]]

===See also===
* [[niinku]]
* [[nääs]]
* [[tiäksä]]

===Anagrams===
* [[kota#Finnish|kota]], [[toka#Finnish|toka]]

